# User guide sync

When you change behavior that end users see or follow, update `USER_GUIDE.md` in the same change.

## Update when you touch

- Signup, email verify, guest limits, or nav destinations
- Gift order flow (pack sizes, notes, address request, checkout)
- CSV import (`/orders/import`, template/example, columns, caps, payment after import)
- Integrations (Salesforce/HubSpot connect, trigger stage, sync, disconnect)
- CRM fields/stage requirements (what must exist or be populated in Salesforce/HubSpot)
- Profile (photo upload, password, account fields shown)
- Profile options unlocked by CRM (monthly billing, card, spending limit, auto-order)

## How to edit

- Keep the guide written for **new users** (steps and plain language)
- Preserve separate sections for **CSV files** and **Connecting to CRM**
- Match live product behavior — do not document planned/unimplemented features
- Prefer the live catalog/API over stale UI copy if they disagree
- Keep the maintainer note at the top of `USER_GUIDE.md`
